# zenrav1e NEON assembly vs pure-Rust fallback — first ARM measurement
date:    2026-07-28
host:    Apple M4 Pro (12 core), macOS, aarch64
build:   release, NO -C target-cpu=native
method:  COMPILE-TIME A/B. zenrav1e's ARM SIMD is hand-written NEON assembly
         under src/arm/, selected by cfg(asm_neon) which build.rs emits when
         the `asm` feature is on. There is no runtime token, so:
           cargo bench --bench tier_isolation --features asm   # neon_asm
           cargo bench --bench tier_isolation                  # rust_fallback
         (cfg(asm_neon) confirmed emitted: target/release/build/zenrav1e-*/output)
input:   noise+patches, still picture, 1 thread, q100, speed preset 8

## Result

| size    | NEON asm  | pure Rust | speedup |
|---------|-----------|-----------|---------|
| 256x256 | 116.15ms  | 156.25ms  |  1.35x  |
| 512x512 | 457.20ms  | 615.55ms  |  1.35x  |

Clean 1.35x, stable across both sizes. No regression.

## Why this bench had to be written

`benches/bench.rs` DOES NOT COMPILE against the current API. It is gated behind
`required-features = ["bench"]`, so no CI job or default `cargo bench` builds
it, and it has drifted:

  error[E0061]: this method takes 7 arguments but 6 were supplied
    --> benches/bench.rs:75  (ts.qc.update)
  error[E0061]: this function takes 25 arguments but 22 were supplied
    --> benches/bench.rs:97

Pre-existing — nothing in this crate's src/ was touched. Until that is
repaired, there was no working measurement of what the NEON assembly buys, on
any architecture. benches/tier_isolation.rs uses only the public encode API, so
it does not drift with internal signatures.

NOT MEASURED: per-kernel attribution. This is whole-encode wall time; which of
the mc / predict / dist / looprestoration assembly routines carry the 1.35x
needs a profile.
